.TH RFS-FUSE 1 "2026" "rfs-fuse" "RFS Manual"
.SH NAME
rfs-fuse \- mount an RFS filesystem image via FUSE
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rfs-fuse
.I image-file mountpoint
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rfs-fuse
mounts an RFS volume (a single image file) as a directory using FUSE. RFS is a
copy-on-write, log-structured, self-healing filesystem: it commits atomically
via a superblock ring, verifies every block against a parent-stored checksum,
and supports snapshots.
.PP
If the image file is empty or does not exist it is created and formatted (64
MiB by default); otherwise the existing volume is reopened. The process runs in
the foreground and serves the mount until unmounted with
.BR fusermount3 (1)
.RB ( "fusermount3 -u " mountpoint ).
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
rfs-fuse /var/lib/rfs/data.img /mnt/rfs &
mkdir /mnt/rfs/docs
echo hello > /mnt/rfs/docs/a.txt
fusermount3 -u /mnt/rfs
.fi
.SH NOTES
Writes become durable on
.BR fsync (2),
on close, and at unmount; unsynced data may be lost on a crash, as POSIX allows.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mount.fuse (8),
.BR fusermount3 (1)
